0..71 Comment "// What a recursion handed through a higher-order function refuses. The"
72..150 Comment "// recursion\'s own parameter handed to `apply` instantiates its type parameter"
151..227 Comment "// at that parameter\'s stage, which the claim does not take (#393). A helper"
228..305 Comment "// whose signature names no type parameter hands its argument on at no stage,"
306..382 Comment "// and a helper with no recursion opens no stage for its result to follow: a"
383..456 Comment "// signature quantified over stages lifts both, the sized rung\'s explicit"
457..530 Comment "// bound (#392). Shared with `../../model/data/sized-higher-order.gandr`."
532..574 Comment "// The naturals the recursions take apart."
